# --- per-target source/sink declaration -------------------------------------
# Sinks come from the host TaintP2X catalog ($TP2X/taint): RemoteCodeExecution,
# ExecArgSink, SQL, SSRFSink, FileSystem_ReadWrite, ExecDeserializationSink, ...
# So usually you only declare the SOURCE here: the entrypoint parameter that
# receives untrusted input. Reuse the existing source kind 'LLMControlled' as a
# generic "attacker-controlled" label so the host rules (LLMControlled -> sink)
# fire without editing taint.config.
#
# Replace the signature below with your target's real untrusted-input entrypoint.
def myapp.web.handle_request(self, request: TaintSource[LLMControlled]): ...
#
# Declare an extra sink ONLY if the host catalog doesn't already cover it, e.g.:
# def myapp.db.raw_query(sql: TaintSink[SQL]): ...
